## Validity

### Load average before each run (1, 5, 15 minutes; the run waited for the 1-minute figure to fall below LOAD_MAX)

| App | Rep | Before | After |
|---|---|---|---|
| theDotNetWay | 1 | 0.78 0.57 1.16 | 3.44 2.34 1.75 |
| theDotNetWay | 2 | 1.25 2.13 1.97 | 3.73 3.15 2.45 |
| theDotNetWay | 3 | 1.29 2.54 2.28 | 4.70 3.40 2.67 |

### Host CPU probe (a fixed spin timed on every pinned CPU, against the quietest this VM has shown; bench/lib/hostprobe.py)

The VM's load average cannot see another program on the Mac taking the cores its vCPUs run on; this can. A ratio of 1.00 is a quiet host, above 1.10 the pinned server and load generator were slowed by something outside the run. `After each window` probes the machine right after every measured run of the rep.

| App | Rep | Before the run | After the run | Windows probed above 1.10 | Highest after a window |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| theDotNetWay | 1 | 1.09 | 1.04 | 0/6 | 1.07 |
| theDotNetWay | 2 | 1.07 | 1.06 | 0/6 | 1.09 |
| theDotNetWay | 3 | 1.07 | 1.05 | 0/6 | 1.08 |

### Responses by status class, every HTTP run of every rep

| App | Route | 2xx | 3xx | 4xx | 5xx | Errors (no response) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| theDotNetWay | room_show | 229,304 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| theDotNetWay | avatar | 2,595,407 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| theDotNetWay | post_message | 75,855 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |

### Warm-up before each measured run (the app runs the route at the measured concurrency until its throughput is flat; bench/lib/warmup.py)

`measured / warm-up tail` is the measured run's requests a second over the mean of the last three 2 s warm-up windows: well above 1 would mean the app was still speeding up when measurement began, well below 1 that it was slowing down.

| App | Route | c | warm-up seconds | settled | measured / warm-up tail |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| theDotNetWay | room_show | 1 | 30.0 [30.0–30.0] | 3/3 | 1.00 |
| theDotNetWay | room_show | 16 | 30.0 [30.0–30.0] | 3/3 | 1.00 |
| theDotNetWay | avatar | 1 | 30.0 [30.0–30.0] | 3/3 | 1.00 |
| theDotNetWay | avatar | 16 | 32.0 [30.0–90.0] | 2/3 **←** | 0.99 |
